    "statement": "In a shortened row (R+s,s,d+s), suppose the line direction differs from a codeword on an e-set with 1<=e<d. Every pair-noncontained witness meets that e-set. After subtracting the codeword direction, each slope gives a codeword in the punctured ordinary list with agreement at least d+s-e, and each punctured codeword owns at most e slopes. Hence |Z|<=e floor(C(R-e+s,s)/C(d-e+s,s)). At the first all-direction-unpaid dimensions this pays e<=5 on KoalaBear and e=1 on Mersenne-31.",
